# Environment-dependent example: reports nginx processes visible in this Linux host.
# Read-only snapshot of every process whose kernel name is exactly nginx.
# show does not send signals or change process state.
# Role of yesh: select and report a bounded process view; the kernel and procfs remain the sources of state.

nginx = processes where name is "nginx"
show $nginx fields pid uid state rss start_time cgroup
summarize $nginx memory rss
